# Heads-up Hold'em's results tree — same rules as `../results/.gitignore`, which
# is the Cheat study's. A SEPARATE tree because `study.py` and `verify.py`
# default to `../results/transcripts`: another game's transcripts inside that
# glob would silently fold poker hands into the published Cheat numbers.
#
# Transcripts are committed GZIPPED (`*.jsonl.gz`); the uncompressed working
# copies a run produces are ignored. Transcripts are NOT regenerable — they
# contain real model responses, which are not deterministic — so the .gz files
# are the record, not a cache. `metrics.iter_jsonl` and `verify.py` read either
# form:
#
#   python -m experiments.llm_eval.verify --game cardlang_holdem_heads_up \
#       --dir experiments/llm_eval/results_holdem/transcripts
*.jsonl
estimate/

# Per-run directories (`runs/<UTC stamp>/`, see layout.py). Their `summary.json`
# IS tracked: it is the only record of what one invocation spent and how far it
# got.
runs/*/figure.png
